<p>Yeah, in my mind there's no passive, vague cause for why 112 is the way it is. Every step of the construction process went as smoothly as making a intended-to-be-country-famous coaster could go. The minute the company's testers started coming back severely weakened and tired, all their expectations went down the toilet.</p>
<p>You've inspired me to perhaps write up an interview from that perspective; the one company tester that lucked into having a short enough subjective ride length (or maybe, she was just a bit more sturdy a person) to basically tell the designers that the ride is horrible. Something that they (mis)translated to &quot;this ride is horrible and unfun&quot; instead of &quot;yeah I was there for X months&quot;.</p>

